note: ### **Gmail OAuth Integration Research Notes**

#### **Developer Portal & App Registration**
*   **Console URL:** [Google Cloud Console](https://console.cloud.google.com/) (APIs & Services > Credentials).
*   **Account Type:** Standard Google Account or Google Workspace account.
*   **Cost:** API usage is generally free within generous quotas. However, **Security Assessments (CASA)** required for Gmail restricted scopes cost between **$540 and $1,000** for the automated self-serve track in 2026 (source: Unipile, CellCog).
*   **Setup:** You must enable the **Gmail API** in the Library before configuring the OAuth consent screen.

#### **OAuth Technical Specs**
*   **Endpoints:**
    *   **Authorize:** `https://accounts.google.com/o/oauth2/v2/auth` (probe)
    *   **Token:** `https://oauth2.googleapis.com/token` (probe)
*   **Discovery:** [https://accounts.google.com/.well-known/openid-configuration](https://accounts.google.com/.well-known/openid-configuration) (probe)
*   **PKCE:** Supported (`S256`).
*   **Redirect URI Rules:**
    *   **HTTPS Required:** Mandatory for all production URIs. `http://localhost` or `http://127.0.0.1` are the only exceptions.
    *   **Exact Match:** N
